+\subsection{Plain-English Flow of the Paper}
+The paper follows one path. First, EchoForge declares what world it is simulating: a public-source fixed-wing pusher-prop positive proxy, benign hard negatives, and sensor/weather/noise stressors. Second, it generates scenario groups and three phase records per group: initial take-up, climb transition, and cruise altitude. Third, it converts synthetic radar and cue products into detector-view features while blocking labels, split fields, group identifiers, and generator internals. Fourth, it evaluates accepted radar/cue baselines and a human-engineered fusion baseline. Fifth, it introduces EI as a train/CV-only sparse-fusion search that writes a lock before one blind holdout pass. Finally, it reports one headline KPI and pushes modeling detail, code listings, and CLI commands into the appendix.
