+\section{Detector-Processing Baselines and Accepted Fusion}
+After synthetic sensing, EchoForge deliberately reduces the generator state to detector-view features. This mirrors a practical radar-evaluation workflow: raw products become branch scores and cue summaries, then fusion methods combine those branch-level outputs. The baseline ladder is intentionally familiar: CFAR/MTD-style radar features, track/cue confidence, acoustic cadence, passive-RF provenance, tabular/sequence ML controls, and a human-engineered late-fusion comparator.
+
